{
 "source": {
  "reference": "https://ai.google.dev/api/live",
  "fetched": "2026-10-12",
  "operation": "WS /ws/google.ai.generativelanguage.v1beta.GenerativeService.BidiGenerateContent",
  "guides": [
   "https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/live-api/get-started-websocket",
   "https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/live-api/capabilities",
   "https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/live-api/tools",
   "https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/speech-generation"
  ]
 },
 "rule": [
  "Each schema transcribes the message of the same name in the Live API reference to the checker's keyword set. A client or server message is an object holding one message kind; enum values stay as the reference spells them; optional members stay optional.",
  "Setup keeps the members the voice sends and tools, which stays open so a planted tool list is judged by the engine's own test, not refused here. generationConfig keeps responseModalities and speechConfig.",
  "Content and Part keep the members a spoken turn carries: text, inlineData and the thought flag. functionCall and the other part kinds are left out: a frame carrying one is built off-schema by the row that proves its refusal.",
  "usageMetadata and voiceActivity sit outside the one message kind, as the reference's BidiGenerateContentServerMessage has them; each kind's message schema lists both.",
  "Transcription keeps the reference's text, languageCode and offsets, and python-genai's finished, which the reference does not list.",
  "usageMetadata, the arguments of a function call and a go-away's time stay open. The checker closes every other object."
 ],
 "omitted": [
  "Client messages the voice does not send: toolResponse, and realtimeInput's video, text, activityStart, activityEnd and audioStreamEnd members.",
  "Setup members the voice leaves unset: contextWindowCompression, sessionResumption, proactivity, the automatic activity detection tuning, turnCoverage and interimTranscriptTimestampEnabled.",
  "serverContent's groundingMetadata and urlContextMetadata, which answer tools the voice never offers, and the media resolution and thinking settings."
 ],
 "schemas": {
